#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:88
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of sysmon3"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:91
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>sysmon3</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:95
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>qmake sysmon3.pro &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:99
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:103
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:106
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>install -vm755 sysmon3 /usr/bin</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:111
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring sysmon3"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:114
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:117
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<filename>$HOME/.config/LinuxFromScratch/&lt;monitored "
"system&gt;.conf</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:121
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The configuration files are created at run time for each system being "
"monitored.  They are not normally updated manually, but are managed by the "
"program's configuration widgets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:127
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"When first run, the program asks for the system to be monitored.  After "
"testing that communication to the server is satisfactory and the server name"
" is saved, the main window will start.  After initial setup, the setup "
"widget can be bypassed by passing the server name as an argument to the "
"program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:135
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The program is designed to take up minimal screen space so by default it "
"does not have a frame.  The frame can be toggled on and off with Ctrl-F.  "
"This can be useful for placing the window in the desired location.  After "
"initial placement, the location is saved in the configuration file for the "
"next time the program is started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/sysmon3.xml:143
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"A short operation menu is brought up with a right mouse click on the main "
"window. Configuration widgets are brought up with F1."
msgstr ""

